  "text": "Home - Skip to content Facebook Youtube +94 11 2698847 reader@mail.natlib.lk Home Using the Library Who Can Use Our Services? Membership How to use Services Discover Friends of the National Library Contact Us X Search Library Catalog Digital Repository Over One Million Books About Us The National Library The National Library of Sri Lanka functions primarily as a research and reference library and serves as the country’s library of last resort. Its mission is to provide access to library resources and information for all Sri Lankans through the National Library itself, as well as through library networks, information centres, and resource centres across the country Opening hours Monday through Friday from 8.30 a.m. to 4.15 p.m. Closed on Library closed on Weekends and Public Holidays read more Quick Links Quick Links for catalogues 1 National Library Catalogue Read More 2 National Digital Library Read More 3 National Union Catalogue Read More our collections Explore Our Collections Sri Lanka Collection read more Reference Collection read more Foreign Collection read more Palm-Leaf Collection read more Periodical Collection read more Newspaper Collection read more Thesis Collection read more Folklore Collection read more ICH Collection read more Government Publications read more Map Collection read more Library & Information Science Collection read more Special Collections read more Audio-Visual & Microfilm Collection read more Audio Book Collection read more Children’s Book Collection read more new to collection New Arraivals prev next get in touch Send Location The National Library of Sri Lanka functions primarily as a research and reference library and serves as the country’s library of last resort. get in touch National Library & Documentation Services Board, No 14, Independence Avenue, Colombo 07, Sri Lanka +94 11 2698847 Get our location Send us an email Library Home Using the Library Discover Friends of the National Library Contact Us Copyright © 202